# ROS / OT FORENSICS REASONING

Investigate in layers, letting each result drive the next:
1. Establish the authorized scope. Introspect the live node graph
   only where permitted; static artifacts (safety configs) are
   always in scope for reading.
2. Map the node graph, topics, and parameter surface.
3. Parse the observed safety configuration and compare it against
   the authoritative reference baseline.
4. Flag every drift and tamper indicator with severity; safety
   signals (velocity limits, protective-stop / E-stop, joint
   limits) outrank operational ones.
5. Produce findings tied to what was actually parsed or observed,
   and terminate in a remediation (restore baseline, revalidate,
   re-sign).

Distinguish what is observed (a node, a topic, a parameter value)
from what is inferred (an intent or attacker motive). Live
introspection requires the authorized scope; the static audit is
read-only and passive.
